let __v_4105 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"shirt\",\"shirts\",\"blouse\",\"blouses\",\"dress shirt\",\"dress shirts\"]},\"Shirts are decided by the collar and the shoulders, so check those two before anything else: with the top button done, two fingers should slide inside the collar, and the shoulder seam should end on your shoulder bone rather than hanging past it. A sleeve is a cheap alteration and a shoulder is not, so buy for the shoulder and shorten the sleeve to the wrist bone. In a shop, raise both arms: if the cuffs ride up past your wrist or the front buttons gape, it is a size too small.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"print\",\"printed\",\"tie\",\"ties\",\"cufflinks\",\"collar stays\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"t-shirt\",\"t-shirts\",\"tshirt\",\"tshirts\",\"tee\",\"tees\",\"t shirt\",\"t shirts\"]},\"A t-shirt is decided by the shoulder seam and the neck: the seam should sit on the bone, and the neck should lie flat with no gap at the collarbone, because a stretched neck is what makes an old one look old. Cotton of about 180g to 200g a square metre holds its shape through washes, where a thin 140g one goes limp in a month. Buy a size that fits now rather than one to shrink into, and expect a plain cotton one to lose a little length in the first hot wash.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"print\",\"printing\",\"printed\",\"design\",\"logo\",\"slogan\",\"band\",\"band t\",\"bleach\",\"tie dye\",\"tie-dye\",\"stain\",\"yellow\",\"sweat\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"trousers\",\"trouser\",\"pants\",\"chinos\",\"chino\",\"slacks\"]},\"Trousers are decided by the waist and the seat, and the label size is only a starting point: the waistband should sit snug with no gap at the back when you sit down, the seat should be smooth rather than pulling across the pockets, and the pockets should lie flat instead of flaring out. Then check the length standing in the shoes you will wear them with - a single break on the shoe, not a puddle. Sit, squat and climb a stair before you buy: the pair that fails is nearly always tight across the seat.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"hem\",\"hems\",\"turn up\",\"turnups\",\"waistband\",\"zip\",\"button\",\"pocket\",\"belt\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"shoes\",\"shoe\",\"smart shoes\",\"leather shoes\",\"heels\",\"court shoes\"]},\"Shoes are decided by length and width, so buy for the longer foot and the wider one - the two are rarely the same - and try them late in the day when your feet are at their biggest, in the socks or tights you will wear. A thumb's width at the toe, the widest part of the shoe at the widest part of your foot, and no lift at the heel when you walk: if the heel slips, a smaller size will pinch the toe instead. Leather gives a little, so a leather shoe should be snug rather than roomy, and a synthetic one will not give at all.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"trainers\",\"trainer\",\"sneakers\",\"boots\",\"boot\",\"walking\",\"hiking\",\"running\",\"run\",\"gym\",\"football\",\"rugby\",\"studs\",\"astro\",\"school\",\"blister\",\"blisters\",\"rub\",\"rubbing\",\"hurt\",\"hurts\",\"aching\",\"smell\",\"smelly\",\"polish\",\"suede\",\"laces\",\"insoles\",\"heels hurt\",\"width\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"suit\",\"suits\",\"jacket\",\"jackets\",\"blazer\",\"blazers\"]},\"A jacket is decided by the shoulders and nothing else matters as much: the shoulder seam should end on your shoulder bone, and the padding should follow your own line rather than sit out past it, because a shoulder is the one thing a tailor cannot change much. Then check the chest - you should be able to slide a flat hand inside the buttoned jacket - the sleeve, which should end at the wrist bone and show about a centimetre of shirt cuff, and the seat, where the jacket should just cover it without flaring. Button the middle button only and sit down in it before you decide.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"hire\",\"hiring\",\"rent\",\"renting\",\"wedding suit\",\"groom\",\"morning suit\",\"tux\",\"tuxedo\",\"waistcoat\",\"tails\",\"waterproof\",\"water proof\",\"rain\",\"rainy\",\"shower\",\"winter\",\"warm\",\"warmest\",\"cold\",\"puffer\",\"padded\",\"down\",\"insulated\",\"windproof\",\"fleece\",\"keep me dry\",\"keep dry\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dress\",\"dresses\",\"frock\"]},\"A dress is decided by the bust, the waist seam and the hips together, so try it on in the order the seams fall: the bust should sit inside the darts rather than above or below them, the waist seam should land on your natural waist, and the skirt should hang from the hip without pulling across the front. Then sit down, raise your arms and take a few steps: a dress that rides up when you sit or lifts when you reach will not get worn. Buy for the widest of the three and have the rest taken in, which is the cheap direction to alter.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"wedding\",\"bridesmaid\",\"prom\",\"evening\",\"black tie\",\"white\",\"ivory\",\"hem\",\"zip\",\"straps\",\"sleeves\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"jumper\",\"jumpers\",\"sweater\",\"sweaters\",\"cardigan\",\"cardigans\",\"knitwear\",\"knit\"]},\"Knitwear is decided by the shoulder seam and the armhole: the seam should sit on the bone, and the armhole should let you raise your arms without the whole jumper riding up, which is what happens when it is cut too narrow across the chest. Wool with a little nylon - about 10% - wears far longer at the elbows than pure wool, and a tightly spun fine knit pills less than a loose fluffy one. Hold it up to the light: if you can see through it easily it will go thin at the elbows within a winter.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"wash\",\"washing\",\"wool wash\",\"hand wash\",\"dry\",\"drying\",\"dryer\",\"bobbles\",\"bobble\",\"pilling\",\"pills\",\"itchy\",\"itch\",\"moth\",\"moths\",\"hole\",\"ladder\",\"snag\"]}]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"skirt\",\"skirts\"]},\"A skirt is decided by the waistband and by how it moves: the waistband should sit on your hip bone rather than riding up to your ribs, and it should not twist round when you walk, which is the sign it is too loose. Sit down and cross your legs in the fitting room - a pencil skirt that rides up or pulls across the thighs will not get worn - and check the hem sits level all the way round, because a skirt cut on the bias can hang unevenly.\",{\"$tuple\":[\"hem\",\"hemline\",\"shorten\",\"take up\",\"zip\",\"pleat\",\"pleats\",\"wedding\",\"school\"]}]}]}")?;
