let __v_4106 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"run\",\"running\",\"jog\",\"jogging\",\"5k\",\"10k\",\"parkrun\",\"marathon\",\"half marathon\"]},\"For running, go to a running shop and let them watch you run: it costs nothing, they fit for how your foot lands, and £90 to £130 buys the pair that stops the injuries a cheap trainer causes. Replace them every 500 to 800km, or when the midsole feels flat under the ball of your foot, and keep a second pair to alternate if you run most days.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"cycling\",\"cycle\",\"bike\",\"commute\",\"pedal\"]},\"For a commute you do not need special shoes: flat pedals with ordinary shoes are fine, and a stiff sole is the only thing that helps on a long ride. Clip-in shoes are worth it only once you ride most days and want the pull on the upstroke - then a mountain-bike style cleat you can walk in beats a road cleat, and budget about £60 with the pedals.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gym\",\"weights\",\"lifting\",\"deadlift\",\"squat\",\"crossfit\"]},\"For the gym, a flat, firm sole is what you want: a cheap canvas plimsoll or a proper lifting shoe keeps you stable under a weight where a cushioned runner wobbles. Save the cushioned pair for running and use the flat one for anything with a bar.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"walking\",\"hiking\",\"hill\",\"hills\",\"trek\",\"mountain\",\"muddy\"]},\"For walking, the boot or shoe should be waterproof with a deep rubber tread and stiff enough under the arch to stop a stone bruising your foot. Try them late in the day in the socks you will walk in, with a thumb's width at the toe and no lift at the heel, and break them in around the house before a long day out.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"standing all day\",\"on my feet\",\"shift\",\"nurse\",\"hospital\",\"warehouse\",\"kitchen\"]},\"For standing all day, put the money into a cushioned sole and room at the toes, and buy at the end of the day when your feet are at their biggest. Two pairs worn alternately last far longer than one, and a snug heel matters more than a soft one.\"]}]}")?;
